if you have tried the new fortnight  limited time event then you'll know that  it's not the easiest task to get that  Golden Glove now I can't tell you how to  get it every time but I can give you  some hints that I found helped me get  the Infinity Gauntlet much more often  the Gorner will spawn inside the preset  circle when you spawn on the map the  objective now is to get as much airtime  as possible  ride the bus to the end of the circle  then jump to pour your shoot and make it  to the middle of the circle as fast as  possible you'll see plenty of people  around you now your objective is to get  just below them but not so low that you  can't do a little skydive at the end you  may have to tap your shoot button again  again to just get a few more feet below  the guy next to you but while being as  low as possible while also having as  much airtime as possible gives you the  best shot at getting the Infinity  Gauntlet you'll hear a noise somewhere  around the two-minute mark the gauntlet  will follow soon after so keep your ears  and eyes open as soon as you hear a  sonic boom you should be able to see the  infinity corner flying in now is the  time to skydive hopefully because you're  in the middle of the circle you'll be in  a good position to get close to the  comet the comet flies fast so aim in  front of it then when you've got the  angle just right point down fall as fast  as possible then your glider should be  able to take you the rest of the way now  this won't work every time since  everyone's their hands on the glove but  it definitely gives you a good fighting  chance you could do extra things like  landing on trees and buildings to drop  down faster too so in summary staying  the sky as long as you can get to the  middle be the lowest parachute to  possible wait for the 2 minute ish mark  fly fast and aim ahead of the comet then  if you're on PC gets the gauntlet and  spam eat as fast as possible if you  still have no luck but still want to  check out Fanus then we have a full  victory royale gameplay video on our  youtube channel so go check that out and  for more for night fun times make sure  you subscribe to gamespot.com  [Applause]
 

